---
import ExternalLink from '../components/ExternalLink.astro';
import { AUTHOR, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Contact"
	description="How to reach Oded Messer - what to reach out about, and where."
>
	<h1>Contact</h1>
	<p>
		Hi there! I'm Oded. A software engineer, architect, and manager with over 13 years of
		experience. Most recently, I led cloud and data at Prisma Photonics, where we used fiber sensing
		to monitor critical infrastructure. Before that, I led engineering at Iterative (now <ExternalLink
			href="https://datachain.ai/">DataChain</ExternalLink
		>), working on MLOps tools including <ExternalLink href="https://dvc.org/">DVC</ExternalLink>,
		{' '}<ExternalLink href="https://cml.dev/">CML</ExternalLink>, and{' '}
		<ExternalLink href="https://github.com/datachain-ai/datachain">DataChain</ExternalLink>.
		Earlier, I worked on data science platform-as-a-service (PaaS) at{' '}
		<ExternalLink href="https://www.iguazio.com/">Iguazio</ExternalLink> (now part of QuantumBlack, AI
		by McKinsey) and Intel. I also do occasional consulting.
	</p>

	<p>Happy to hear from you. Here is the best way to reach me.</p>

	<h2>Get in touch if…</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Something I wrote was wrong, or you have a better counter-example.</li>
		<li>
			You want to chat about distributed systems, software architecture, MLOps, AIOps or to
			philosophize about software futurism.
		</li>
		<li>
			You have an unusual engineering leadership problem, need advice or want to compare notes.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Where</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>LinkedIn DM</strong> - <ExternalLink href={AUTHOR.linkedin}>
				linkedin.com/in/odedmesser
			</ExternalLink>. Best for anything short.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Email</strong> - <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Best for
			anything long, or anything with an attachment.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>GitHub</strong> - <ExternalLink href={AUTHOR.github}>
				github.com/omesser
			</ExternalLink>. Issues and PRs on anything of mine.
		</li>
	</ul>
</BaseLayout>
